{"created": "2021-01-17T18:35:59.048987+00:00", "modified": "2021-03-25T12:18:53.549013+00:00", "id": 4446043, "conceptrecid": "4437019", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4446043", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.4437019", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4446043", "metadata": {"title": "Determinants of Airbnb prices in European cities:  A spatial econometrics approach (Supplementary Material)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4446043", "publication_date": "2021-01-13", "description": "<p>This repository contains supplementary materials for the article:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Determinants of Airbnb prices in European cities: &nbsp;A spatial econometrics approach</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>(</strong>DOI<strong>:&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tourman.2021.104319\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tourman.2021.104319</a>)</p>\n\n<p>The materials include the used datasets and Python&nbsp;scripts for spatial regression models.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Datasets</strong></p>\n\n<p>For each city two files are provided: data for weekday&nbsp;and weekend offers</p>\n\n<p>The columns are as following:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>realSum: the full price of accommodation for&nbsp;two people&nbsp;and two nights in EUR</li>\n\t<li>room_type: the type of the accommodation&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>room_shared: dummy variable for shared rooms</li>\n\t<li>room_private: dummy variable for private rooms</li>\n\t<li>person_capacity: the maximum number of guests&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>host_is_superhost: dummy variable for superhost status</li>\n\t<li>multi: dummy variable if the listing belongs to hosts with 2-4 offers</li>\n\t<li>biz: dummy variable&nbsp;if the listing belongs to hosts with more than 4 offers</li>\n\t<li>cleanliness_rating: cleanliness rating</li>\n\t<li>guest_satisfaction_overall: overall rating of the listing</li>\n\t<li>bedrooms: number of bedrooms (0 for studios)</li>\n\t<li>dist: distance from city centre in km</li>\n\t<li>metro_dist: distance from nearest metro station in km</li>\n\t<li>attr_index: attraction index of the listing location</li>\n\t<li>attr_index_norm: normalised attraction index (0-100)</li>\n\t<li>rest_index: restaurant&nbsp;index of the listing location</li>\n\t<li>attr_index_norm: normalised restaurant&nbsp;index (0-100)</li>\n\t<li>lng: longitude of the listing location</li>\n\t<li>lat: latitude of the listing location</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Programming&nbsp;Scripts</strong></p>\n\n<p>In this repository you will find a script for spatial regressions in Python using PySAL (models_robust.py).</p>\n\n<p>The codes cover the following regression models:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>OLS</li>\n\t<li>SLX (lagged_x)</li>\n\t<li>SAR (lagged_y)</li>\n\t<li>SDM (lagged_x_y)</li>\n\t<li>SEM (lagged_e)</li>\n\t<li>SDEM (lagged_e_x)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Main parameters:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>cities - list of cities from the dataset to be included in the analysis</li>\n\t<li>Robust=False: calculate the OLS, SLX, SAR and SDM regressions with W (weight matrix) based on 10 closest neighbours</li>\n\t<li>Robust=True: calculate all regression models with different specifications of W</li>\n\t<li>direct_indirect=True: calculate the direct and indirect effects (based on Golgher, A. B., &amp; Voss, P. R. (2016). How to Interpret the Coefficients of Spatial Models: Spillovers, Direct and Indirect Effects. Spatial Demography (Vol. 4). https://doi.org/10.1007/s40980-015-0016-y)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Key functions:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>create_weights - defines the W specification</li>\n\t<li>write_stats - calculates&#39;s Moran&#39;s I and Geary&#39;s C</li>\n\t<li>direct - calculates the direct effect of the variable</li>\n\t<li>indirect - calculates the indirect effect</li>\n\t<li>coord - sets the coordinate refence system (CRS) appropriate to the analysed city</li>\n\t<li>total_results calculates the regressions</li>\n\t<li>the coordinates are projected from GPS (epsg:4326) to the local CRS (km_lat, km_lon)</li>\n\t<li>all regressions are saved as formatted txt table</li>\n\t<li>the results can be also saved as csv table</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Gy\u00f3di, Krist\u00f3f", "affiliation": "University of Warsaw", "orcid": "0000-0003-2999-8444"}, {"name": "Nawaro, \u0141ukasz", "affiliation": "University of Warsaw", "orcid": "0000-0003-1995-4894"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "4437019"}}]}, "notes": "This research was supported by National Science Centre, Poland: Project number 2017/27/N/HS4/00951"}, "title": "Determinants of Airbnb prices in European cities:  A spatial econometrics approach (Supplementary Material)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4446043", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4446043?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4446043", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4446043", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.4446043", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4437019", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4437019", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4437019", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.4437019", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:4446043/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:4446043/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4446043/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https: